<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n53891" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καταδεύω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>wet through</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατέδευσας ἐπὶ στήθεσσι Χιτῶνα οἴνου
					ἀποβλύζων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					9.490
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μήποτέ σ᾽ . . νέφος ἀμφικαλύψῃ . .
					κατά θ᾽ εἵματα δεύσῃ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hes.
					<u>Op.</u>
					556
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἵν᾽ οὔατα μὴ καταδεύῃ</span>
			that [the rain] <i>may</i> not <i>wet</i> your ears, ib.<i><span class="en">
				546
			</span></i>; of a river, <i>water</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πεδίον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Ph.</u>
					827
				</span></i>
			 (anap.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			metaph., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ -όμενος τῇ καρδίᾳ</span>
			he whose heart <i>is easily melted</i>, <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Ex.</u>
				35.5
			</span></i>.</div>
